&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineer, Enterprise Platforms, you will be a hands-on owner of the collaboration tools our employees use all day. You will administer, automate, and improve them, working alongside identity, endpoints, and the wider SaaS stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who sees a problem, figures out the fix, and ships it. Our team is small and the scope is broad. You will have real ownership early, a lot of autonomy, and few layers between you and the people you support. You will turn policies, runbooks, and employee needs into reliable configurations, scripts, and self-service experiences. We use AI tools where they make us faster or more accurate, and we expect good judgment about when to trust them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reflects Abnormal VOICE values. You move with velocity, design for long-term ownership and governance, use data with intellectual honesty, stay close to customer needs, and aim for excellence in reliability and simplicity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Google Workspace: users, groups, org units, shared drives, Drive sharing and DLP, Gmail routing and policies, Calendar and room resources, Meet, and audit and security investigation tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Slack (Enterprise Grid): workspaces, channels, user groups, permissions, app approvals, Slack Connect, retention, export and eDiscovery, workflows, and audit logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain automation for joiner, mover, and leaver flows, access requests, deprovisioning, and common employee needs, using SCIM, APIs, webhooks, Apps Script, and scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with identity (Okta SSO, MFA, group-based access) so Google and Slack access follows least privilege and birthright rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support endpoints and other SaaS platforms as needed, including macOS device management and long-tail SaaS administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create self-service experiences, runbooks, and enablement content so employees can resolve common needs without escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Tier 2/3 incidents, perform root cause analysis, and feed what you learn back into automation, runbooks, and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add logging, dashboards, and reporting so changes are monitored and audit questions can be answered quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools where they help (documentation, troubleshooting, request triage, analysis), with human review and appropriate access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security, GRC, Legal, People, Finance, and IT Service Delivery to deliver changes safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage incoming requests and incidents by impact and urgency, route them to the right owner or queue, and resolve or escalate within agreed response targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn vague or incomplete requests into clear requirements: ask clarifying questions, identify stakeholders and constraints, and confirm the desired outcome before building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations with employees and stakeholders about scope, timelines, and tradeoffs. Give status updates proactively, and flag risks or delays early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce standards for external sharing, Slack Connect, guest access, and third-party and OAuth app approval in Google Workspace and Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular access and license reviews, using systems and audit logs to find unused, orphaned, or over-privileged access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep configuration baselines documented, changes tracked in ServiceNow, and evidence ready for SOC 2, ISO 27001, and FedRAMP audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review audit logs and investigate suspicious activity with Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document requirements, risks, and approvals for changes so they pass change review and can be audited later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scripting and Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate first. If a task happens more than a couple of times, you script it, build a workflow, or turn it into self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write scripts and tools (Python, Apps Script, and shell) against the Google Workspace, Slack, and Okta APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations and workflows in Workato, connecting identity, HR, collaboration, ticketing, and SaaS systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Torii workflows to automate app discovery, onboarding and offboarding, and license reclamation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build ServiceNow catalog items and flows so requests are routed, approved, and fulfilled with minimal manual touch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep scripts and configuration in version control, with logging, error handling, and clear documentation so others can run and maintain them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Google Workspace, Slack (Enterprise Grid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; Okta&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation and integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Workato, Torii, Python, Apps Script&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service management:&lt;/strong&gt; ServiceNow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoints and other:&lt;/strong&gt; Jamf, Zoom, and a long tail of SaaS applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need experience with every tool. Strong experience with comparable platforms, and a record of learning new ones quickly, is what matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation-first:&lt;/strong&gt; We remove repetitive work rather than absorbing it, and we measure success by manual touches eliminated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-first:&lt;/strong&gt; Employees are our customers. We respond with urgency, communicate clearly, and fix root causes so the same problem doesn&#39;t come back. We do what we say we&#39;ll do, or we tell people early when that changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-paced:&lt;/strong&gt; Priorities shift quickly and requests arrive from every direction. We move fast, ship in small steps, and iterate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time management and triage:&lt;/strong&gt; You juggle incidents, requests, and project work. You sort what comes in by impact and urgency, handle what&#39;s urgent first, and protect focused time for project work and for the root-cause fixes that prevent tomorrow&#39;s tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You find the problem before someone assigns it, and you follow through to a documented, working fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with ambiguity: unclear requirements, incomplete documentation, and shifting priorities don&#39;t stop you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You prioritize well when everything feels urgent. You set expectations early and honestly: you say no or &quot;not yet&quot; clearly and kindly, and you explain the reason.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You learn new platforms quickly and teach what you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You ask the right questions up front: who needs this, what problem it solves, what &#39;done&#39; looks like, and what could go wrong. You propose a recommended approach rather than waiting to be told.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate proactively: status updates, change notices, and honest post-incident write-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in IT engineering, systems administration, or a similar role supporting business-critical technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on administration of Google Workspace (Admin console, groups, Drive and sharing controls, Gmail, Calendar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on administration of Slack (workspace and channel management, user groups, app management, permissions). Enterprise Grid experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of identity and access concepts: SSO, MFA, least privilege, directory and group management, and SCIM or standards-based provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to script and integrate systems using APIs, webhooks, Apps Script, Python, or similar tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with incident and change management, troubleshooting, root cause analysis, and documented follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including documenting technical processes and explaining complex systems to non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of working independently and taking ownership without close direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing scripts or building workflows that automate repetitive IT work, and a habit of automating before doing something manually a third time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first approach to supporting employees: responsive, clear, and focused on fixing root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and manage your time across incidents, requests, and project work, prioritizing by impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to set and manage expectations with stakeholders, including saying no or negotiating scope and timelines while keeping trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a startup or high-growth company, where you wore multiple hats, built processes from scratch, or scaled IT through rapid headcount growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with acquisitions, tenant or domain migrations, or workspace consolidation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data governance in collaboration tools: retention, legal hold, eDiscovery, DLP, and audit log analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Workspace or Slack administration certifications, or involvement in their admin communities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Okta, Jamf, Zoom, or other enterprise SaaS administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in remote-first, SaaS-first, or zero-trust environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with version control, configuration-as-code, or CI/CD for platform automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building self-service workflows, or using AI tools to improve support, troubleshooting, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of security and compliance frameworks (SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP) as applied to collaboration and end-user platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workato or a similar integration platform (Zapier, Tray.io, Boomi, or Okta Workflows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Torii or another SaaS management platform, such as Zluri or BetterCloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ServiceNow (catalog items, flows, incident, request, and change) or a similar ITSM platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Microsoft 365 (Entra ID, Exchange Online, Teams, SharePoint/OneDrive, or the M365 admin center), especially in a mixed Google and Microsoft environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-AA1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on AI in our process:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Abnormal AI uses AI-assisted tools to help our recruiting team prepare for candidate interviews. These tools analyze resume content and role requirements to suggest interview questions and areas for the interviewer to explore.They do not make hiring decisions or screen candidates automatically. Every decision about a candidacy is made by a person. Further, if your application is successful and Abnormal AI makes a conditional offer of employment, we will carry out pre-employment checks which must be successfully completed to progress to a final offer. All processes and pre-employment checks are in line with prevailing legislation and Abnormal AI&#39;s policies relevant to our security and privacy standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. For our EEO policy statement please &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt9cbda641db7c0045/6a1e3d3a66aea075cd33e462/AAP_and_EEO_Statement.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;click here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. If you would like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt4eb3a265cc7b1ca9/6a1e3d3bfe33e73c16ff026b/EEOC_Know_Your_Rights_Oct_30_2025.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The secret to our success lies in our connectivity, while operating with a high degree of flexibility. Work-life balance remains our priority while feeling connected is important to maintain our strong culture, achieve our goals, and thrive as #OneJamf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do at Jamf:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Inside Account Executive is a key member of the EMEIA sales team, helping existing customers and channel partners understand how they can make the management and the security of their Apple devices robust and easy. The role works with the extended sales team to hit individual targets as well as contributing to the overall MEA sales goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role is offered as hybrid, with the expectation to be in the office in Amsterdam Zuid 3 days per week. We are only able to accept applications for those based in the NL and have sponsorship to live and work in the NL #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What you can expect to do this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regularly with a defined list of existing accounts throughout the year to identify areas of need for business growth and new solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own on-time renewal for your entire SMB customer portfolio; consistently meet or exceed retention rate targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively engage customers 90–120 days ahead of renewal to understand health, flag risks, and secure commitment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customer business needs and schedule technical demonstrations or face to face meetings with SE as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and qualify upsell and cross-sell opportunities within the existing customer base by aligning Jamf solutions to customer business needs and industry insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute campaigns to drive traffic to online and in-person events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enter new Opportunities and related information into SalesForce.com to document and manage sales activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop well-rounded understanding of JAMF sales&amp;nbsp;philosophy, market and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know how to position JAMF Software solutions against competitor offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately process customer transactions such as price quotations and purchase orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow understanding of and ability to explain business value of JAMF Software solutions to prospects and existing customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for leading and closing sales opportunities for the Strategic Commercial team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs all job responsibilities in alignment with the core values,&amp;nbsp;mission and purpose of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adheres to the highest moral, ethical and legal standards to deliver an environment that promotes respect, innovation and creativity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports and promotes a positive, inclusive workplace one in which the talents and strengths of our increasingly diverse workforce are welcomed, further developed and manifested in our work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English is required and Arabic is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2+ years of experience in a sales, business or entrepreneurial role (required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General Experience selling in both direct and indirect (channel) models (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General Experience navigating and negotiating legal agreements (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General Experience in software sales within high-growth technology companies (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and coordinate well with other team members that are remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interact effectively with prospects and customers via phone and email&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance areas of responsibility across multiple territories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10% travelling expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SECURITY AND PRIVACY REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;markedContent&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in ongoing security training is mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established security protocols will be adhered to, sensitive data will be handled responsibly, and data protection practices are followed, including understanding relevant privacy regulations and reporting breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acknowledging the Jamf Code of Conduct, where applicable security and privacy policies can be found, is a requirement of all roles at Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Why Jamf?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;Named a 2025 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;Named a 2025 Newsweek America’s Greatest Workplaces for Gen Z&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;Named one of Forbes Most Trusted Companies in 2024&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;Named a 2024 Newsweek America’s Greatest Workplaces for Parents &amp;amp; Families&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;Named a 2024 PEOPLE Companies That Care by PEOPLE® and Great Place To Work®&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;We offer a clear and defined sales career path. Our main goal is to help you successfully step into our Account Executive role, but there are many ways to advance your career at Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;We train and then we give you the room to grow. Our Jamfs can explore the vertical career path, as well as the horizontal, to discover new interests and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;You don’t have to be a techie to be a Jamf. Our best-in-class sales focused Bootcamp training provides you with the technical and product knowledge required to confidently talk with customers about Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;We set achievable targets, help each other out, and share best practices across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;9313&quot;&gt;You will have the opportunity to make a real and meaningful impact for more than 75,000 global customers with the best Apple device management solution in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it means to be a Jamf?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We are a team of free-thinkers, can-doers, and problem-crushers. We value humility and the relentless pursuit of knowledge. Our culture flows from a spirit of selflessness and relentless self-improvement - driving both personal growth and collective progress throughout our company. We unite around common goals while respecting personal approaches, believing that fulfilled individuals create a thriving, vibrant workplace.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our aim is simple: hire exceptionally good people who are incredibly good at what they do and let them do it. We provide the support and resources to let everyone be their authentic, best selves at work, at rest, and at play. We are committed to supporting the continual improvement of Apple in the workplace, the organizations that rely on them and the people who keep it all running smoothly.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above it all, waves our banner of #OneJamf – and the knowledge that when we stand together, we accomplish so much more than we could alone. We seek individuals who share this unwavering journey toward growth to join us in our quest for constant improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does Jamf do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Jamf extends the legendary Apple experience people enjoy in their personal lives to the workplace. We believe the experience of using a device at work or school should feel the same, and be as secure as, using a personal device.&amp;nbsp;With Jamf, customers are able to confidently automate Mac, iPad, iPhone and Apple TV deployment, management, and security – anytime, anywhere – to protect the data and applications used by employees in the workplace, students learning in the classroom, and streamline communications in healthcare between patients and providers.&amp;nbsp;More than 2,500 Jamf strong worldwide, we are free-thinkers, can-doers, and problems crushers who are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work each and every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get social with us and follow the conversation at #OneJamf&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
